\section{Experiments}

\subsection{Recorded Calculation and Error Definitions}

This section reports the single deterministic calculation in the experimental log. For an added scalar $b$, define the target-prediction difference as $e_i(b)=y_i-(2x_i+b)$. The two reported errors are
\[
\operatorname{MAE}(b)=\frac{1}{5}\sum_{i=1}^{5}|e_i(b)|,
\qquad
\operatorname{MSE}(b)=\frac{1}{5}\sum_{i=1}^{5}e_i(b)^2.
\]
The recorded settings are $b=0$, $1.5$, and $3$. The intermediate setting $b=1.5$ is a supplied partial correction; only $b=3$ equals the observed mean residual. These settings are neither stochastic runs nor optimization steps. No optimizer, external dataset, external baseline method, timing result, or held-out evaluation is supplied.

